---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Text from "@/components/fundations/elements/Text.astro";
import Wrapper from "@/components/fundations/containers/Wrapper.astro";
---

<BaseLayout>
  <section>
    <Wrapper variant="standard" class="py-12">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-y-8">
        <div class="lg:pr-8">
          <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-20 lg:z-50">
            <Text
              tag="h3"
              variant="textBase"
              class="text-base-900 font-display"
            >
              About FW.VISION
            </Text>
            <div
              class="relative before:absolute after:absolute before:bg-base-950 after:bg-base-950/10 before:top-0 before:left-0 before:h-px before:w-6 after:top-0 after:right-0 after:left-8 after:h-px pt-4 mt-2 flex flex-col gap-4"
            >
              <div>
                <Text
                  tag="h4"
                  variant="textSM"
                  class="text-base-900 font-medium"
                >
                  Institutional Foresight Architecture
                </Text>
                <Text tag="p" variant="textXS" class="text-base-600 mt-2">
                  FW.VISION is a founder-led AI-native think tank. It publishes open, citable frameworks for long-horizon institutional design, governs strategic funds using those frameworks, and incubates ventures that operationalise them.
                </Text>
              </div>
              <div>
                <Text
                  tag="h4"
                  variant="textSM"
                  class="text-base-900 font-medium"
                >
                  The Thesis
                </Text>
                <Text tag="p" variant="textXS" class="text-base-600 mt-2">
                  AI enables companies of tens to outperform companies of thousands. FW.VISION operates as its own case study in this thesis: a small human core orchestrating a fleet of specialised AI agents to produce institutional-scale research, governance, and advisory.
                </Text>
              </div>
              <div>
                <Text
                  tag="h4"
                  variant="textSM"
                  class="text-base-900 font-medium"
                >
                  50-Year Horizon
                </Text>
                <Text tag="p" variant="textXS" class="text-base-600 mt-2">
                  FW.VISION operates on a 50-year return horizon. The firm champions long-term thinking as the foundational practice of sovereign innovation, structuring governance and investment for enduring futures rather than quarterly cycles.
                </Text>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div
              class="relative before:absolute after:absolute before:bg-base-950 after:bg-base-950/10 before:top-0 before:left-0 before:h-px before:w-6 after:top-0 after:right-0 after:left-8 after:h-px pt-4 mt-4"
            >
              <Text tag="h4" variant="textSM" class="text-base-900 font-medium"
                >Engage</Text
              >
              <Text tag="p" variant="textXS" class="text-base-600 mt-2">
                FW.VISION offers consulting workshops, governance advisory, and foresight infrastructure design.
              </Text>
              <div class="mt-4">
                <Text
                  tag="a"
                  variant="textXS"
                  href="mailto:francis.wang@fw.vision"
                  class="text-base-600 hover:underline"
                  >francis.wang@fw.vision</Text
                >
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div
          class="lg:col-span-3 lg:pl-8 lg:relative lg:before:absolute lg:after:absolute
          lg:before:bg-base-950 lg:after:bg-base-950/10 lg:before:top-0
          lg:before:left-0 lg:before:h-6 lg:before:w-px lg:after:top-8
          lg:after:bottom-0 lg:after:left-0 after:w-px"
        >
          <Wrapper
            variant="prose"
            class="text-sm text-base-600 max-w-xl mx-auto"
          >
            <div>
              <Text tag="h2" variant="displaySM" class="text-base-900 font-display font-medium">
                Three Pillars
              </Text>

              <div class="mt-8">
                <Text tag="h3" variant="textBase" class="text-base-900 font-display font-medium">
                  1. Futures Research and Scenario Formulation
                </Text>
                <p class="mt-2">
                  Evaluating possibilities through the Foresight Scope (APPETITE model). Formulating futures worth actualising. Publishing scenarios, frameworks, and signal analysis. This is the intellectual engine: open infrastructure that propagates through adoption and citation.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="mt-8">
                <Text tag="h3" variant="textBase" class="text-base-900 font-display font-medium">
                  2. Strategic Fund Governance
                </Text>
                <p class="mt-2">
                  Providing long-horizon governance architecture to strategic funds pursuing specific futures: food sovereignty, digital independence, climate resilience, innovation infrastructure. Governance frameworks reduce risk and extend time horizons, enabling larger, more resilient fund structures.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="mt-8">
                <Text tag="h3" variant="textBase" class="text-base-900 font-display font-medium">
                  3. Venture Studio Incubation
                </Text>
                <p class="mt-2">
                  Owner-operator model for early ventures. Two-tier structure: Horizon Studio (internal ideation, hypothesis testing, partner recruitment) feeds Futures Foundry (independent portfolio entity with equity-based partnerships). Every venture uses the same governance frameworks FW.VISION publishes and governs with.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="mt-12">
                <Text tag="h2" variant="displaySM" class="text-base-900 font-display font-medium">
                  Founder
                </Text>
                <div class="mt-4">
                  <Text tag="h3" variant="textBase" class="text-base-900 font-medium">
                    Francis Wang
                  </Text>
                  <p class="mt-2">
                    12 years building and governing ventures at scale. Exits at $70M and $650M across technology, energy, and digital infrastructure. Doctoral candidate in Design researching innovation ecosystems and institutional architecture for sovereign innovation.
                  </p>
                  <p class="mt-2">
                    Francis operates FW.VISION as the commercial application of validated intellectual infrastructure: frameworks developed through personal research (published at findcongwang.com) are adopted as proprietary governance tools for institutional clients.
                  </p>
                  <p class="mt-2">
                    The firm is deliberately AI-native: a fleet of trained AI agents operates as the primary research and production workforce, governed by the same CITAble framework published in the FW.VISION lexicon. This is not a future aspiration. It is the current operational model.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="mt-12">
                <Text tag="h2" variant="displaySM" class="text-base-900 font-display font-medium">
                  Proprietary Frameworks
                </Text>
                <p class="mt-4">
                  FW.VISION develops, publishes, and governs with a growing corpus of proprietary frameworks:
                </p>
                <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2">
                  <li><a href="/lexicon/citable-framework" class="text-accent-600 hover:underline">CITAble</a> - Operational framework for organisational legibility</li>
                  <li><a href="/lexicon/citable-business-index" class="text-accent-600 hover:underline">CITAble Business Index</a> - Integrating meta-index for a future-proof venture</li>
                  <li><a href="/lexicon/cognitive-vitality-index" class="text-accent-600 hover:underline">Cognitive Vitality Index</a> - The cognition axis of Hybrid Intelligence</li>
                  <li><a href="/lexicon/agentic-gradient" class="text-accent-600 hover:underline">Agentic Gradient</a> - The AI-adoption axis of Hybrid Intelligence</li>
                  <li><a href="/lexicon/societal-resilience-index" class="text-accent-600 hover:underline">Societal Resilience Index</a> - Whether a venture stabilises the society it depends on</li>
                  <li><a href="/lexicon/active-futuring" class="text-accent-600 hover:underline">Active Futuring</a> - Moving toward a future rather than waiting for it</li>
                  <li><a href="/lexicon/appetite-model" class="text-accent-600 hover:underline">APPETITE Model</a> - Eight-dimension futures scenario analysis</li>
                  <li><a href="/lexicon/strategy-citemap" class="text-accent-600 hover:underline">Strategy CITEMap</a> - Visual strategy exploration tool</li>
                  <li><a href="/lexicon/hybrid-intelligence" class="text-accent-600 hover:underline">Hybrid Intelligence</a> - Human-centric, agentic scale</li>
                  <li><a href="/lexicon/key-shaped-talent" class="text-accent-600 hover:underline">Key-Shaped Talent</a> - Talent model for the AI era</li>
                  <li><a href="/lexicon/founder-led-organisation" class="text-accent-600 hover:underline">Founder-Led Organisation</a> - AI-native micro-institution architecture</li>
                </ul>
              </div>

              <div class="mt-12">
                <Text tag="h2" variant="displaySM" class="text-base-900 font-display font-medium">
                  Thinking and Actualizing
                </Text>
                <p class="mt-4">
                  FW.VISION explores the underlying possible trajectories of the future: it formulates scenarios, evolves them as signals change, and judges which futures are worth actualizing. It does not build the ventures itself.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-2">
                  Operational partners actualize the futures worth building. SyncID Labs hosts the projects that become ventures, and the funds that host ventures innovating in alignment with the trajectories FW.VISION theorises. FW.VISION thinks and governs; the operational arm actualizes.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-2">
                  Both run on the same intellectual property: Hybrid Intelligence, the practice of human-centric agentic scale, and the CITAble assessment that measures whether a venture is future-proof. FW.VISION uses the CITAble framework to assess businesses and ensure strategic alignment of futures.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="mt-12">
                <Text tag="h2" variant="displaySM" class="text-base-900 font-display font-medium">
                  Market Category
                </Text>
                <p class="mt-4">
                  <strong>Institutional Foresight Architecture.</strong> A new category at the intersection of system design, sovereign innovation, and founder-led governance. FW.VISION is the only organisation that publishes open, citable frameworks for long-horizon institutional design, governs strategic funds using those frameworks, and incubates ventures that operationalise them.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </Wrapper>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Wrapper>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
